7. Why Does Printing PriorityQueue Directly Not Show Treatment Order?
Printing a PriorityQueue directly does not guarantee sorted output.

A priority queue guarantees that the highest-priority element is available at its head. It does not guarantee that all elements are stored in sorted order.

To display the correct treatment order, we create a copy of the queue and repeatedly use poll() on that copy.

This displays the patients in priority order without modifying the original waiting list.
